	(text_box "MCP2221A\n\nSynopsis: \n\n	USB 2.0 to I2C/UART Protocol Converter with GPIO\n\nDatasheet: \n\n	https://ww1.microchip.com/downloads/en/DeviceDoc/20005565C.pdf\n\nInfo:\n\n	MCP2221A is a USB composite device that uses industry-standard USB classes:\n\nFor the UART (Serial) side: \n\n	Linux automatically uses the standard cdc_acm driver. \n	It will show up as a virtual serial port, typically named /dev/ttyACM0 or /dev/ttyACM1.\n\nFor the I2C, GPIO, ADC, and DAC side: \n\n	The chip operates as a standard USB HID (Human Interface Device).\n	Linux communicates with it directly via the standard hidraw interface (driver).\n\nStandby Current: \n	Typical 46 uA\n\nOperating current:\n	Typical 10 mA, max 12 mA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 128.27 26.67 0)
		(size 113.03 61.1979)
